libarc_support 1.1.0
====================

libarc_support supplies the ARC and Blocks runtime functions needed by
applications which still support Mac OS X 10.4 and later.  PowerPC, i386 and
x86_64 are supported.  The x86_64 slice requires Mac OS X 10.5 or later.  The
static library is the recommended product.

Using it in an Xcode project
----------------------------

1. Drag libarc_support.xcodeproj into your project.
2. Add libarc_support_static as a target dependency.
3. Link libarc_support.a to your application target.

That is all.

The libarc_support_dylib target builds libarc_support.dylib for applications
which prefer a dynamic library.

CMake users may add this directory with add_subdirectory() and link either
libarc_support::static or libarc_support::dynamic.  For example:

    add_subdirectory(path/to/libarc_support)
    target_link_libraries(MyApplication PRIVATE libarc_support::static)

Building and testing
--------------------

Open libarc_support.xcodeproj and build libarc_support_static or
libarc_support_dylib.  Build the check target to run both the native runtime
tests and the ARC code-generation tests.

Use ARCHS=ppc when building the PowerPC slice with a PowerPC-capable
toolchain.  Xcode 4.2 on Snow Leopard builds the i386 and x86_64 slices.

The library itself is compiled without ARC.  Application source may use ARC
and Blocks normally with a compatible Clang compiler.

